# ANV-0053 -- the P6 audit could not see a split that had left its parent
# keys in a parent's pending-split payload have no live replica holding them,
# so the audit counted them unreachable and the bank short
seed        = 4 (serializable), 6 (snapshot-isolation)
workload    = txn_bank, kind = bank
nodes       = 5
faults      = drawn from seed; needs a split in flight when the audit runs,
              which this phase's churn profile makes near-certain
invariant   = conservation (the bank total)
reproduce   = anvil_txn_faults 30
note        = disproved as an engine bug by measurement: the same seed with a
              longer settle window reported total=1600/1600 at 40s, 60s, 90s
              and 200s, while the topology kept churning underneath. Money that
              reappears when you look later was never missing. Fixed by giving
              the transactional audit the same pending-split walk P5's
              audit_conservation has always had.
